<!--Post: 1676--><!--Time: 1102583262-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1676"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 09, 2004 - 1:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The photo of the baby with the beaver/boxing gloves &#40;speculated&#41; on it&#39;s sweater looks like Shirley Vian. <BR> <BR>A lot! <BR> <BR>If you super-impose the two photos over each other they match up. <BR> <BR>Look at their noses.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1676-->
<!--Post: 4433--><!--Time: 1106358360-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4433"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 5:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree Q. In fact soon after the picture arrived someone from KSNW - TV posted a message at a genealogy site requesting information. Sadly, it has never been answered. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.genforum.genealogy.com/vian/messages/107.html" target=_top>http://www.genforum.genealogy.com/vian/messages/10 7.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4433-->
<!--Post: 4434--><!--Time: 1106359272-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4434"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Curious2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Curious2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 6:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Essevi - Her children went to live with her <BR>first husband in Texas.  I believe in Honey Grove, or Powderly, Texas. And I think one other <BR>child lives in Okalhoma.  This thread is <BR>interesting because I also think the baby <BR>looks like Shirley.  And ironically, with <BR>that &#34;Curly Q&#34; on the top of her head, that <BR>is probably why BTK wrote that poem, &#34;Shirley <BR>Locks, Shirley Locks&#34; to WPD. &#40;instead of  <BR>Curly Locks, Curly Locks.&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4434-->
<!--Post: 4447--><!--Time: 1106367332-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4447"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Debbie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Debbie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 8:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t believe Shirley was ever married to the Vian fellow. Her former married name was Relford and that&#39;s what name is on her tombstone. So, I doubt anyone in the Vian forum at the genealogy site would know her. Her maiden name was Lawson - maybe if someone looked up the Lawson forum and posted the picture there...I think it looks like her, also.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4447-->
<!--Post: 4450--><!--Time: 1106369298-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4450"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Curious2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Curious2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 8:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You are right.  Shirley was &#34;common law&#34; married  <BR>to Richard Vian.  Her children&#39;s last name is <BR>Relford, which was her first husband&#39;s last name.  And, yes, her maiden name was Lawson; but <BR>her children go by their father&#39;s last name - <BR>Relford.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4450-->
<!--Post: 8354--><!--Time: 1109087951-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8354"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Raidar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Raidar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 7:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am not doubting anyones opinon on the picture looking like Vian. I think there is a simularity myself also. BTK might have took the picture from her. But...i have been married,have children to and it is hard for me to understand that her children/husbands&amp;friends do not recognize it. I think if it were her they would know. I have seen baby pictures from my friend,husband and even his family and he has mine to.Even if they havent seen that exact picture they would know her from another one. Just a thought..  <BR> <BR>RAIDAR<!--/Text--></td></tr>
